
### 10.2 Earlier campaigns of this increment: historical, invalid for the 11-scenario gate

Three runs were made before the report above and are kept as history, not as evidence of this gate. (1) `e9c6bac`, gate of seven scenarios (tag `evidence/go-campaign-e9c6bac` and its release): valid for that gate, incomplete for this one. (2) `8b64ad5` and `cc786e4`, gate of eleven scenarios: **GMdup invalid**, S18 concurrent in timeout in 28 to 29 of 30 runs; cause, from the logs: the S18 gate closed its release channel unconditionally, GMdup delivers the last chain message twice, the second `close` panicked inside the watcher and the watcher stopped before it handled `Terminated`. It was a defect of the judge harness under duplicated messages, not of the runtime. The harness now releases the gate once (`sync.Once`, `judge_internal_test.go`), its assertions and the detection criterion are unchanged, and no retry was added. (3) `2eea4b6`: 12 of 12 met, superseded by the campaign of the tree that contains the final README. (4) `7937c9e`: 12 of 12 met on the tree before the port fixes of slice 6; valid history, no longer current once `watch_test.go` changed the tree of `pekko-actor/` (tag `evidence/go-campaign-7937c9e`, local). Their directories are preserved with their logs and manifests.

